      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested — Please split this CL** and address the inline comments.\n\n### Review Summary\n\n**Functionality:** `Flash()` in `rts5817_flasher.cc` currently relies on the caller (`main()` in `rts5817_flash.cc`) to strip the DFU suffix and reject an empty payload before calling `Flash()`. If `Flash()` is called directly with an empty buffer or a 16-byte suffix-only image, it opens the device, enables download mode, detaches the hardware into DFU mode (`0BDA:5800`), waits for re-enumeration, and only then fails inside `DfuDownload()` with `RtsError::kInvalidParameter` — leaving the device in DFU mode.\n\n**Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** Co-locating `StripDfuSuffix()` and the empty-payload check at the start of `Flash()` in `rts5817_flasher.cc` (before `OpenTarget()`) makes `Flash()` self-validating, keeps `rts5817_flash.cc` as thin CLI glue, and makes the pre-flight suffix stripping and empty-payload rejection directly testable in `rts5817_flasher_test.cc`. Exposing `kDetachTimeout`, `kReEnumTimeout`, and `kReEnumPollInterval` in `rts5817_flasher.h` (matching `rts5817_usb_device.h`) also allows tests to reference those constants directly.\n\n**Code Simplicity:**\n- In `rts5817_flash.cc`, the single-use `Report()` helper and its unnamed namespace can be replaced with a direct `std::println(stderr, ...)` call.\n- In `rts5817_flasher.cc`, `dfu_id` is hoisted outside the `if (!in_dfu_mode)` branch where it is used.\n- In `rts5817_libusb_backend.cc`, `Open()` uses raw pointer temporaries (`raw_list` and `handle`) where `std::out_ptr(list)` and `std::out_ptr(dev_handle_)` can be used directly (matching `Init()` and `GetInterfaces()` in the same file), and the two `namespace { ... }` blocks can be merged.\n- In `rts5817_flasher_test.cc`, `#include \u003cstring\u003e`, `using ::testing::Not;`, `FakeBus::get_status_calls`, and `FakeBus::init_count` are unused.\n\n**Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** In `rts5817_flasher_test.cc`, prefer `std::ranges::fill(data, 0)` over `std::fill(data.begin(), data.end(), 0)` and C++23 `std::ranges::contains(bus_-\u003eevents, event)` in `Saw()`, and replace the hardcoded `milliseconds(100)` and `1 \u003c\u003c 20` literals with expressions derived from `kReEnumTimeout` and `kReEnumPollInterval`.\n\n**Testing:**\n- `rts5817_flasher_test.cc` is missing tests for the early-return error paths when `EnableDownload()` or `DfuDetach()` fails in `Flash()`, for DFU suffix stripping and empty/suffix-only payload rejection, and for the exact re-enumeration poll timeout boundary (`kReEnumTimeout / kReEnumPollInterval - 1` vs. `kReEnumTimeout / kReEnumPollInterval`).\n- `PollsUntilTheDfuDeviceAppears` uses `EXPECT_GE` instead of asserting the exact sleep duration (`EXPECT_EQ(slept_, 2 * kPolls * kReEnumPollInterval)`).\n- `RtsLibusbBackend` (`rts5817_libusb_backend.cc`) is not linked into `rts5817_flash_test` and has no unit tests for its uninitialized/unopened guard paths.\n\n**Security:** N/A\n\n**CL Size \u0026 Scope:** `Size: L (+950, -1)`. The non-test production delta is 512 lines (`rts5817_libusb_backend.{h,cc}`: 266 lines, `rts5817_flasher.{h,cc}`: 141 lines, `rts5817_flash.cc`: 86 lines, `build.mk`: 19 lines) alongside 438 lines of unit tests (`rts5817_flasher_test.cc`), exceeding the 250-line production limit and bundling three independently reviewable and testable components. Please split this CL into smaller stacked CLs (continuing the pattern of the parent CLs in this stack):\n1. **CL 1 (`RtsLibusbBackend`):** Add `util/realtekfp/rts5817_libusb_backend.{h,cc}` and `util/realtekfp/rts5817_libusb_backend_test.cc`, wired into `rts5817_flash_test` in `util/realtekfp/build.mk`.\n2. **CL 2 (`rts5817_flasher`):** Add `util/realtekfp/rts5817_flasher.{h,cc}` and `util/realtekfp/rts5817_flasher_test.cc`, wired into `rts5817_flash_test` in `util/realtekfp/build.mk`.\n3. **CL 3 (`rts5817_flash` CLI binary):** Add `util/realtekfp/rts5817_flash.cc` and the `rts5817_flash` host binary target in `util/realtekfp/build.mk`.\n\n**Commit Message:** Well-written prose with proper `BUG\u003d` and `TEST\u003d` tags; when splitting the CL, scope each commit message to its corresponding layer:\n\n*CL 1 commit message:*\n```text\nrts5817: Add libusb backend for RtsUsbBackend\n\nAdd RtsLibusbBackend, the libusb-1.0 implementation of RtsUsbBackend\nfor the RTS5817 host flashing tool.\n\nThe backend enumerates devices with libusb_get_device_list() rather\nthan using libusb_open_device_with_vid_pid(), so a device that exists\nbut cannot be opened is reported as access denied instead of missing.\n\nBUG\u003db:494586772\nTEST\u003dmake BOARD\u003dhost utils-test\n```\n\n*CL 2 commit message:*\n```text\nrts5817: Add firmware flashing sequence\n\nAdd Flash() in rts5817_flasher.{h,cc} to orchestrate the RTS5817 DFU\nupdate flow independently of the command line so that it can be unit\ntested against a simulated USB bus.\n\nFlash() strips any trailing DFU suffix, rejects empty payloads before\ntouching USB, enables download mode and detaches runtime devices into\nDFU mode, flashes devices already in DFU mode directly without\ndetaching again, and waits for the device to re-enumerate in runtime\nmode after the download completes.\n\nBUG\u003db:494586772\nTEST\u003dmake BOARD\u003dhost utils-test\n```\n\n*CL 3 commit message:*\n```text\nrts5817: Add rts5817_flash command line tool\n\nAdd the rts5817_flash host utility entry point wiring command-line\nparsing, firmware file reading, RtsLibusbBackend, and Flash() into a\nself-contained flashing binary.\n\nBUG\u003db:494586772\nTEST\u003dmake BOARD\u003dhost utils-test\nTEST\u003dRun ./rts5817_flash -i ec_rts5817.bin against an RTS5817 device;\nDFU download completes and the device boots the new image.\n```\n\n[[trajectory](https://goto.corp.google.com/traj/101a2012-b605-4679-9305-0c22661e65c3)]",
