      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Two improvements in `Flash()`:\n\n1. **Co-locate `StripDfuSuffix()` and the empty-payload check at the start of `Flash()`:** Currently `rts5817_flash.cc` strips the DFU suffix and checks `firmware.empty()` in `main()`, while `Flash()` itself opens the target device, enables download mode, sends `DfuDetach()`, and waits for DFU re-enumeration before `DfuDownload()` checks `firmware.empty()`. Calling `Flash()` with an empty span or a 16-byte suffix-only image therefore detaches the device into DFU mode (`0BDA:5800`) before failing with `RtsError::kInvalidParameter`, and keeping the pre-flight check in `main()` leaves it untested by `FlasherTest`. Moving `StripDfuSuffix()` and `if (firmware.empty())` to the top of `Flash()` makes `Flash()` self-validating before touching the USB bus.\n2. **Narrow variable scope:** `dfu_id` (line 70) is only used inside the `if (!in_dfu_mode)` branch, and `in_dfu_mode` (line 69) is only used once as the branch condition.\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, RtsError\u003e Flash(RtsUsbDevice\u0026 device,\n                                    const std::optional\u003cUsbDeviceId\u003e\u0026 requested,\n                                    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e image) {\n  // The device does not accept the DFU suffix as download payload.\n  const std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e firmware \u003d StripDfuSuffix(image);\n  if (firmware.size() !\u003d image.size()) {\n    std::println(\"Stripped {}-byte DFU suffix, payload is {} bytes.\",\n                 image.size() - firmware.size(), firmware.size());\n  }\n  if (firmware.empty()) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"Error: the firmware image is empty.\");\n    return std::unexpected(RtsError::kInvalidParameter);\n  }\n\n  auto target \u003d OpenTarget(device, requested);\n  if (!target) {\n    return std::unexpected(target.error());\n  }\n\n  // A device that is already in DFU mode must not be asked to enter it again:\n  // GET_STATUS stalls there and DFU_DETACH would leave DFU mode instead.\n  if (target-\u003epid !\u003d kRts5817DfuId.pid) {\n    if (auto res \u003d device.EnableDownload(); !res) {\n      return res;\n    }\n\n    // Switch from Runtime mode to DFU mode; the device re-enumerates.\n    if (auto res \u003d device.DfuDetach(kDetachTimeout); !res) {\n      return res;\n    }\n\n    // Poll for the re-enumeration instead of sleeping a fixed time.\n    const UsbDeviceId dfu_id \u003d {.vid \u003d target-\u003evid, .pid \u003d kRts5817DfuId.pid};\n    if (auto res \u003d\n            device.WaitForDevice(dfu_id, kReEnumTimeout, kReEnumPollInterval);\n        !res) {\n      return res;\n    }\n  }\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/101a2012-b605-4679-9305-0c22661e65c3)",
