      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Please tighten the sleep and timeout boundary assertions and add tests for the remaining branches in `Flash()`:\n\n1. **Assert exact sleep duration in `PollsUntilTheDfuDeviceAppears` (lines 294–302):** `polls_before_reenumeration \u003d 3` applies to both detach transitions (Runtime -\u003e DFU and DFU -\u003e Runtime), and `FakeBus` does not sleep during `DfuPollIdle`. Use `EXPECT_EQ` with `kReEnumPollInterval` instead of `EXPECT_GE` with a hardcoded `milliseconds(100)`:\n```cpp\nTEST_F(FlasherTest, PollsUntilTheDfuDeviceAppears) {\n  constexpr int kPollsBeforeReenum \u003d 3;\n  Start(FakeBus::Mode::kBootRom);\n  bus_-\u003epolls_before_reenumeration \u003d kPollsBeforeReenum;\n\n  ASSERT_TRUE(Run({1, 2}));\n\n  // Each of the two re-enumerations (to DFU and back to runtime) sleeps once\n  // per failed poll.\n  EXPECT_EQ(slept_, 2 * kPollsBeforeReenum * kReEnumPollInterval);\n}\n```\n2. **Test the exact re-enumeration poll timeout boundary (lines 414–435):** Instead of `1 \u003c\u003c 20`, derive the poll limit from `kMaxReEnumPolls \u003d static_cast\u003cint\u003e(kReEnumTimeout / kReEnumPollInterval)` (`100`) and verify both sides of the boundary (`kMaxReEnumPolls - 1` succeeds on the final poll; `kMaxReEnumPolls` fails with `RtsError::kTimeout` after sleeping `kReEnumTimeout`).\n3. **Cover the remaining error and pre-flight branches in `Flash()` (`rts5817_flasher.cc` lines 73–80):**\n   - `EnableDownload()` failure (e.g., when `GET_STATUS` in Boot ROM mode fails, `Flash()` returns the error without sending `DFU_DETACH`).\n   - `DfuDetach()` failure (when the initial `DFU_DETACH` fails, `Flash()` returns the error without polling for DFU re-enumeration or downloading).\n   - DFU suffix stripping (an image ending with a valid 16-byte `\"UFD\"` suffix flashes only the payload bytes) and empty / suffix-only image rejection (`Run({})` and `Run(kOnlyDfuSuffix)` fail with `RtsError::kInvalidParameter` and `EXPECT_TRUE(bus_-\u003eevents.empty())`).\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/101a2012-b605-4679-9305-0c22661e65c3)",
